<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Problem Formulation</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we first define the problem of targeted UI automation, and how to convert it into a equivalent classical planning problem.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Problem Definition</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the structure of the app modeled as a UTG, we can now formally define the task of UI automation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(UI Automation)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UI automation is the process of programmatically executing a sequence of actions <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\langle a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{N}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\langle a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{N}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where each action <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we focus on a specific, goal-oriented variant of this task.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Targeted UI Automation)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an app with an initial UI <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{init}</annotation></semantics></math> and a target UI <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{target}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{target}</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective is to find a valid sequence of actions <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\langle a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{N}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\langle a_{1},a_{2},\dots,a_{N}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=(w_{i},e_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=(w_{i},e_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, that navigates the app from <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{init}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{target}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{target}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">We formulate targeted UI automation as a pathfinding problem on the UTG</span>.
Let <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:\mathcal{A}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be a cost function that assigns a
positive cost to each action, representing computational resources, execution time,
or other relevant metrics. The problem is then to find a path from <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{init}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{target}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{target}</annotation></semantics></math>
that minimizes the total execution cost:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}=\arg\min_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\kappa(a_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>π</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=\arg\min_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\kappa(a_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">To simplify the formulation, in this work, we adopt a uniform action cost. This reduces the cost-minimization task to the classical shortest path problem, where the objective is to find the path from <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{init}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{init}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{target}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{target}</annotation></semantics></math> with the fewest actions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_figure ltx_lstlisting ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Listing 1: </span>Domain PDDL for targeted UI automation.</figcaption>
<div id="LST1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_java ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;--ltx-border-color:#000000;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
